{title: Thou Didst Leave Thy Throne}
{artist: Emily E. S. Elliott}
{genre: Christmas}
{style: Hymn}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: G}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 3/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Thou didst leave Thy throne and Thy [D]kingly crown
[G]When Thou camest to earth for [D]me
But in [G]Bethlehem's home was there [C]found no room
For Thy [G]holy nativ[D]ity[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O [C]come to my [G]heart, Lord [D]Jesus
There is [G]room in my [D]heart for [G]Thee
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Heaven's arches rang when the [D]angels sang
[G]Proclaiming Thy royal de[D]gree
But of [G]lowly birth didst Thou [C]come to earth
And in [G]great humil[D]ity[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]The foxes found rest, and the [D]bird its nest
In the [G]shade of the cedar [D]tree
But Thy [G]couch was the sod, O Thou [C]Son of God
In the [G]desert of Gal[D]ilee[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Thou camest, O Lord, with the [D]living word
That should [G]set Thy people [D]free
But with [G]mocking scorn and with [C]crown of thorn
They [G]bore Thee to Cal[D]vary[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]When heaven's arches shall [D]ring, and her choirs shall sing
At Thy [G]coming to vic[D]tory
Let Thy [G]voice call me home, saying [C]Yet there is room
There is [G]room at My side for [D]thee[G]
{end_of_verse}
